# npl-hormones - reference-page UX direction for the three display modes.
# Authored by the tag nitpick lane, 2026-10-14. Not yet generated.
schema: "0.4"
id: npl-hormones-reference-ux
type: image
quality: high
prompt:
  text: |
    Design board for a reference-documentation page, dark theme (deep
    navy-charcoal surfaces, near-white text, muted slate secondary text,
    blue accent). The page documents a synthetic hormone-meter source
    element: seven named drives, each drawn as one horizontal bar with a
    numeric readout and a small delta arrow. The board shows THREE stacked
    example sections, one per display mode, each with a small mode label
    above it. No marketing chrome, no navigation, no browser window -
    documentation panels on a flat dark page.

    Section 1 - mode "panel" (default): a table-like stack of rows, one per
    drive; each row is a short mono uppercase symbol (MTM, TNS, RST), the
    drive name, a slim rounded horizontal bar filled proportionally in the
    blue accent on a faint track, a right-aligned mono numeric value, and a
    small delta arrow after the value (up arrow tinted green, flat dash
    muted, down arrow tinted red). Below the rows, two quiet secondary-text
    lines: a compound state sentence and a triggered line. One row (RST,
    restlessness) is fired: it carries a thin accent-colored left edge bar
    and a barely-there accent tint behind the row, while its text stays at
    full brightness - the highlight points, it never dims or occludes.

    Section 2 - mode "bars": the same rows only, no state or triggered
    lines, slightly tighter vertical rhythm - the compact form for embedding
    in running text.

    Section 3 - mode "alert": two threshold cards stacked with a small gap.
    Each card: a one-pixel warning-red-tinted border, a warning-tinted left
    edge, a faint red tint background, a monospace headline like
    "RST 8.5 >= 7 - strategy-switch" in the warning tint, and one plain
    sentence of body text at full contrast below it ("Restlessness threshold
    crossed. Initiating plan-of-action."). The warning color lives in the
    border, edge and headline only - body text is ordinary foreground.

    Typography: monospace for symbols, values, thresholds and mode labels;
    a clean neutral sans for drive names and body sentences. Generous but
    regular spacing; hairline borders; small border radii (4-6px). Everything
    must read as quiet instrumentation in a spec document, not as a game HUD
    or a biotech illustration.
  negative: |
    Light theme; white background; glossy gradients; neon cyberpunk glow;
    game HUD frames; radar, gauge or sparkline charts; pie charts; organic
    imagery of any kind (molecules, glands, syringes, DNA helices, liquid);
    mascots; logos; watermarks; navigation bars; browser chrome; more or
    fewer than the three named sections; dimmed, strikethrough or occluded
    text anywhere; a fired row rendered disabled; alert cards filling solid
    red; modal dialogs or toast popups.
  style: |
    Flat minimal dark technical documentation, minimal-tech aesthetic,
    instrumentation-panel restraint, hairline rules, monospace accents,
    WCAG AA contrast on all text.
attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-hormones/npl-hormones-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-hormones/npl-hormones-render-390.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-hormones/npl-hormones-ex2-render-390.png
    role: reference
output:
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: npl-hormones-reference-ux.png
eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    mode-coverage:
      weight: 0.3
      description: Exactly three sections labelled panel, bars, alert; bars omits state lines; alert shows cards only.
      fail_signals:
        - "only one or two sections visible"
        - "sections unlabelled or mislabelled"
        - "bars section shows state or triggered lines"
    row-anatomy:
      weight: 0.3
      description: Rows read symbol, name, proportional bar, numeric value, delta arrow in that order; fired row highlighted without dimming its text.
      fail_signals:
        - "bar missing or not proportional to value"
        - "delta arrows absent or all the same color"
        - "fired row dimmed or unreadable"
    theme-match:
      weight: 0.25
      description: Dark minimal-tech surfaces, hairline borders, mono and sans split as specified, AA-legible text throughout.
      fail_signals:
        - "light background anywhere"
        - "neon glow or gradient gloss"
        - "body text below AA contrast"
    no-invented-chrome:
      weight: 0.15
      description: No gauges, radar, sparklines, browser chrome, nav, logos, or organic imagery.
      fail_signals:
        - "any gauge or radar chart"
        - "molecule, syringe, or helix imagery"
        - "browser or window frame"
  reject_if:
    - "image is light-themed overall"
    - "any organic or biotech illustration appears"
    - "fewer than three mode sections"
tags:
  - semtext
  - npl-hormones
  - reference-design
  - dark-ui
